Frequently Asked Questions
1. What is Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)?
Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) is the strategy of formatting and refining website copy so generative AI models like ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Google AI Overviews can easily process, trust, and quote it as a reference source.
2. Does GEO make traditional SEO obsolete?
No. GEO builds upon foundational SEO principles including site indexability, authority signals, and structured data. Traditional SEO ensures your content gets indexed, while GEO earns you placement in AI answers.
3. How can brands track their AI citations?
You can track mentions manually by entering target prompts into engines like Perplexity and Google AI Overviews, or by using specialized AI tracking platforms that monitor automated brand references over time.
4. Is Schema markup necessary for GEO?
Yes. Structured data markup (like Article, FAQ, and Organization schemas) gives explicit context to machine algorithms, dramatically improving extraction efficiency.
5. Why do AI Overviews sometimes cite lower-ranking websites?
AI tools value directness, clarity, and logical formatting over standard SERP positions. A lower-ranking page that offers a clean, concise response often beats out a higher-ranking page filled with fluff.
6. Should small and local businesses invest in GEO?
Yes. AI platforms regularly highlight hyper-focused, well-documented local expertise. Smaller companies providing detailed, specific insights can easily outperform major corporate brands in generative responses.
